stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> BOOT

  BOOT: ST_BOOT
  BOOT: motors commanded OFF first
  BOOT: ADC self-test on all 5 channels

  DISARMED: ST_DISARMED
  DISARMED: motors coasting
  DISARMED: LED slow blink 1 Hz

  ARMED: ST_ARMED
  ARMED: 3 s countdown
  ARMED: LED fast blink
  ARMED: controller state reset

  RACING: ST_RACING
  RACING: closed-loop line following
  RACING: LED solid

  FAULT: ST_FAULT
  FAULT: motors coasting, latched
  FAULT: LED urgent blink 5 Hz

  BOOT --> DISARMED: self-test PASS
  BOOT --> FAULT: self-test FAIL
  DISARMED --> ARMED: ARM button
  ARMED --> RACING: countdown expires
  RACING --> FAULT: line lost > 2500 ms
  RACING --> DISARMED: ARM pressed (soft abort, testing only)
  FAULT --> DISARMED: ARM button (manual reset)

  note right of RACING
    The hardware E-STOP is deliberately
    NOT a state here. It opens the battery
    positive line, so it removes power from
    the MCU and the H-bridge at once and
    cannot be defeated by firmware.
  end note
